{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30315 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool is implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate, which in turn target CCF-STTG1. This indicates a potential pathway where Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool influences the activity of these intermediates, which then modulate CCF-STTG1. The presence of multiple targets for the same starting entity suggests a complex regulatory network, possibly involving enzymatic or metabolic pathways. The integration of these relationships highlights the role of Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool in a broader regulatory cascade that ultimately affects CCF-STTG1. The mechanism is likely mediated through the interaction of Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool with enzymes or metabolites that subsequently influence CCF-STTG1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
